  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1214 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nDeep upper level troughing remains this weekend over the eastern\nthird of the country, keeping weekend temperatures below normal\nwith highs in the low to mid 50s and lows in the mid to upper \n20s. Winds are light as surface high pressure drops southward \ntowards the Quad State. A currently narrow ridge over the Plains\nbroadens through early week. A cutoff upper level low in the \nDesert Southwest tracks towards the Deep South for early next \nweek, keeping conditions locally dry. \n\nAs the broadening surface high moves east early next week, a\nmore southerly flow brings in a warming trend for much of next\nweek, with temperatures returning to normal midweek and then \nabove normal Friday/Saturday. A low pressure system develops in \nthe Front Range around Wednesday, but then tracks to the Upper \nMidwest. With Gulf moisture disconnecting from this system \nThursday, the Quad State should continue to be dry. A \nsubsequent Rocky Mountain system, however, may bring rain \nchances next weekend.",
